        "contents": {
          "markdown": "The [fiction piece](http://www.newyorker.com/fiction/features/2009/05/04/090504fi_fiction_hareven) in this week's *New Yorker* deals with some of the same themes as Eliezer's \"[Three Worlds Collide](http://www.overcomingbias.com/2009/01/three-worlds-collide.html)\"; viz., the clash of value systems (and the difficulty of seeing those with a different value system as rational), and the idea of humanity developing in ways that seem bizarre/grotesque/evil to us."
